                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d28d5379-0e84-4613-a483-a75e3526b3fa",
                        "source_entry_id": "dfcddf09-ec47-32b5-bba2-0cb418023f4d",
                        "source_sense_id": "cb70e547-6f63-36b6-a178-b563382dbd41",
                        "source_sense_description": "Medizin: Störung des Geburtsverlaufs",
                        "target_lang_word": "dystocia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dystocia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa460eb1-6d17-378d-bb80-f9644d5c4ce7",
                                        "entry_id": "50321f1f-c91e-312a-a4db-1c10199b90ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A slow or difficult labour or delivery."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27d51150-c4f1-4d04-a49a-5697b899bc04",
                                                "sense_id": "fa460eb1-6d17-378d-bb80-f9644d5c4ce7",
                                                "text": "In macaques, baboons and chimpanzees, dystocia because of breech birth is the commonest category of fetal death.[…]Breech dystocia is rarely a problem for mother or neonates in small, multitocus species like marmosets and tamarins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21144edf-9153-4547-a1fe-c5f48bdcca91",
                                                "sense_id": "fa460eb1-6d17-378d-bb80-f9644d5c4ce7",
                                                "text": "Dystocia is defined as difficult delivery. Pelvic dystocia is due to aberrations of the pelvic architecture and its relationship to the presenting fetal part.[…]Fetal dystocia may be due to excessive fetal size from gestational diabetes or congenital anomalies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "642571af-34b8-4390-9e9c-61b0aa336780",
                                                "sense_id": "fa460eb1-6d17-378d-bb80-f9644d5c4ce7",
                                                "text": "Although fetal dystocias are sometimes relieved by manipulation and instrumentation, cesarean sections are often the only practical methods of treatment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cea5dcfe-ba82-44bf-8f19-eca7221bb7e8",
                                                "sense_id": "fa460eb1-6d17-378d-bb80-f9644d5c4ce7",
                                                "text": "It is an appropriate way to allow resolution of the dystocia, after clearing the airway and checking for a nuchal cord.\nThe prevailing thinking is that the time window in which to resolve a shoulder dystocia before asphyxial insult (not injury) is about 4 minutes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60e97680-d5ce-4738-abda-021913cab58a",
                        "source_entry_id": "dfcddf09-ec47-32b5-bba2-0cb418023f4d",
                        "source_sense_id": "cb70e547-6f63-36b6-a178-b563382dbd41",
                        "source_sense_description": "Medizin: Störung des Geburtsverlaufs",
                        "target_lang_word": "dystocie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dystocie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "028b7bf4-f058-345b-9271-59a602819e99",
                                        "entry_id": "364f9672-81e1-3438-8cb8-3dc704a82258",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Difficulté lors de l’accouchement pour les femmes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e22e0486-149e-47ca-bf4e-86d6cdd1d535",
                                                "sense_id": "028b7bf4-f058-345b-9271-59a602819e99",
                                                "text": "La dystocie des épaules se caractérise par l’absence d’engagement des épaules après expulsion de la tête."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ca32a34-6eab-4013-9953-15e03a46f1b1",
                                                "sense_id": "028b7bf4-f058-345b-9271-59a602819e99",
                                                "text": "Le mot dystocie a été employé par Hippocrate, Sauvage, Merriman Désormeaux et M. Velpeau, pour désigner l’ensemble des circonstances qui obligent l’accoucheur d’intervenir d’une manière quelconque pour la terminaison de l’accouchement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "42dc6e79-7a7c-3b76-b768-0354012ca031",
                                        "entry_id": "364f9672-81e1-3438-8cb8-3dc704a82258",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Difficulté lors de la mise bas chez les femelles mammifères."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Médecine vétérinaire"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb5f9bd2-28c4-43e9-8c0d-dcf4ad357312",
                                                "sense_id": "42dc6e79-7a7c-3b76-b768-0354012ca031",
                                                "text": "Dominante de la pathologie obstétricale des dernières semaines de l’antepartum, le prolapsus vaginal peut revêtir une forme enzootique lors de la réunion de plusieurs facteurs favorisants : gestation multiple, manque d’exercice, ration alimentaire volumineuse, carence en zinc ou phosphore, dystocie lors des saisons précédentes, terrains en pente, râteliers trop hauts, etc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
